// spec: LEX-031
//
// The string below opens on line 10 and is never closed.  LEX-031 requires the
// diagnostic to name line 10 -- the one place the fault certainly is.  It names
// line 16 instead: the line the scan reached, which is the end of the file.
//
// The four filler lines exist to separate the two, so that a fix is visible in
// the recording rather than being a difference of one.

WriteLn ('oops);

WriteLn ('filler');
WriteLn ('filler');
WriteLn ('filler');
WriteLn ('filler');
